          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "2901735832": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "A workspace is an organizational unit within an organization. Organizations can contain multiple workspaces, and each workspace can house numerous Plasmic projects. Organization members can be added to workspaces or individual projects. For example, you could have an organization for your agency with separate workspaces for each client, or an organization for your company with workspaces for each department.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "2901735833": {
          "values": {},
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "2901735835": {
          "values": {},
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "2901735837": {
          "values": {},
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "2901735839": {
          "values": {},
          "mixins": [],
          "__type": "RuleSet",
          "animations": null
        },
        "2901735848": {
          "tpl": [{ "__ref": "2901735819" }],
          "__type": "RenderExpr"
        },
        "2901735849": {
          "tpl": [{ "__ref": "2901735821" }],
          "__type": "RenderExpr"
        },
        "2901735851": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "What's the difference between private and public users?",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "2901735852": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "Public users can sign in to any project that allows public sign-in, while private users need special permission to access certain projects. If your project has sensitive info, you'll want to use private sign-in to keep things secure.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "2901735853": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "How are users counted?",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "2901735857": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "We keep track of users by their unique email addresses, and it doesn't matter how many devices they use to log into your Plasmic project. Also, we only count active users—potential users in your Users table won't affect your total.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "2901735858": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "What is a collaborator?",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "2901735861": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "Collaborators can build and edit Plasmic applications in your workspace. There are two types: workspace collaborators, who can access all applications in the workspace, and guest collaborators, who can only access specific applications they've been invited to.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "2901735863": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "How are pageviews counted?",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "2901735866": {
          "markers": [],
          "text": "We use built-in analytics to count the number of unique views across any page of your website featuring a Plasmic design. This only applies to content delivered via the Headless API, not codegen.",
          "__type": "RawText"
        },
        "2901735871": {
